1
00:00:44,252 --> 00:00:47,964
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

2
00:00:57,265 --> 00:01:00,852
<i>Does Baraka come to you in your dreams?</i>

3
00:01:02,187 --> 00:01:03,897
<i>No matter how long I wait…</i>

4
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:07,567
<i>Baraka doesn't appear in my dreams.</i>

5
00:01:09,402 --> 00:01:13,031
<i>For me, that's the most painful part.</i>

6
00:01:21,915 --> 00:01:25,251
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

7
00:01:28,379 --> 00:01:30,882
FINALE

8
00:01:56,866 --> 00:01:57,700
You're awake.

9
00:01:59,828 --> 00:02:04,541
There's something I wanted to ask you
before the surgery. But for you to answer…

10
00:02:11,673 --> 00:02:12,966
I'll need to take that off.

11
00:02:13,591 --> 00:02:17,637
You see, you have to remove it,
before trying to smother someone.

12
00:02:17,720 --> 00:02:20,181
And that kid says
he wants to become a doctor.

13
00:02:20,807 --> 00:02:21,641
SYSTEM SHUTTING DOWN

14
00:02:22,016 --> 00:02:26,187
First, you turn the monitor off like this,
then you remove the mask.

15
00:02:26,729 --> 00:02:27,981
What was he thinking?

16
00:02:29,482 --> 00:02:31,609
He's not that kind of person, though.

17
00:02:33,403 --> 00:02:36,322
The kind who truly sets
his mind to getting revenge…

18
00:02:37,282 --> 00:02:43,163
for his pain, profoundly satisfying
revenge on the person who's responsible.

19
00:02:44,497 --> 00:02:49,043
He would never draw up a plan,
and meticulously carry it out.

20
00:02:53,381 --> 00:02:55,091
That's not the kind of person he is.

21
00:02:56,676 --> 00:03:00,054
All he could do was hold
a pillow over the devil's face.

22
00:03:03,224 --> 00:03:07,937
He's so naive, he's not capable
of exacting revenge properly.

23
00:03:09,939 --> 00:03:10,940
However…

24
00:03:16,905 --> 00:03:17,989
I'm not him.

25
00:03:30,960 --> 00:03:32,921
I'll start the dissection now. Bovie.

26
00:03:36,674 --> 00:03:41,471
FLUMAZENIL: A REVERSAL AGENT USED
TO WAKE A PATIENT FROM CERTAIN SEDATIVES

27
00:03:43,765 --> 00:03:46,768
I want to be there in the OR.
Why won't you allow it?

28
00:03:48,728 --> 00:03:52,190
What's the reason?
Why do I have to stay in the donor's OR?

29
00:03:55,693 --> 00:03:56,945
I want to go in too.

30
00:04:00,031 --> 00:04:02,659
I can't let you two go in there alone.

31
00:04:02,742 --> 00:04:05,536
Why do you keep insisting? Do you realize…

32
00:04:07,664 --> 00:04:09,624
Do you really need to be part of this?

33
00:04:10,708 --> 00:04:11,709
Yes.

34
00:04:12,293 --> 00:04:13,336
I won't let it go.

35
00:04:14,754 --> 00:04:17,840
You two are doing this
because you won't let it go either.

36
00:04:24,264 --> 00:04:26,307
After this, your careers are over!

37
00:04:30,270 --> 00:04:34,774
I know that you think this surgery
will be the last one for the two of you.

38
00:04:36,401 --> 00:04:39,320
You don't know how many more kids
like me are out there.

39
00:04:39,404 --> 00:04:41,531
And since you can't bring him to justice,

40
00:04:41,614 --> 00:04:44,242
you're going into that OR
and risking it all!

41
00:04:45,743 --> 00:04:47,495
That doesn't seem fair to me.

42
00:04:50,039 --> 00:04:51,374
So I'll risk it all, too.

43
00:04:53,126 --> 00:04:54,919
Let's go do this together.

44
00:05:03,761 --> 00:05:09,183
My dream, Doctor. Gye Su-jeong, my dream.

45
00:05:09,726 --> 00:05:11,519
<i>Become doctor.</i>

46
00:05:23,406 --> 00:05:24,615
Your hands…

47
00:05:26,617 --> 00:05:28,369
are the hands of a doctor.

48
00:05:28,453 --> 00:05:29,412
They should be used…

49
00:05:31,456 --> 00:05:32,790
to save lives.

50
00:05:39,088 --> 00:05:42,342
This is a desperate attempt.

51
00:05:42,425 --> 00:05:45,053
One that's made in memory of those
who needed help,

52
00:05:46,220 --> 00:05:49,682
<i>those we let slip away and couldn't save.</i>

53
00:05:52,101 --> 00:05:54,187
And at this point, things are up to us.

54
00:05:55,480 --> 00:05:57,315
We desperately need to do something.

55
00:05:59,609 --> 00:06:00,985
No matter the cost.

56
00:06:11,496 --> 00:06:12,622
I, uh…

57
00:06:18,544 --> 00:06:19,712
Hmm.

58
00:06:21,589 --> 00:06:24,217
I was thinking about the timing…

59
00:06:24,300 --> 00:06:25,676
I mean, um…

60
00:06:26,511 --> 00:06:28,596
the sequence of events back then.

61
00:06:31,015 --> 00:06:34,644
That if I had known about it sooner…

62
00:06:36,020 --> 00:06:39,148
I mean, you might not…

63
00:06:39,899 --> 00:06:42,443
Um… I…

64
00:06:44,070 --> 00:06:48,658
I might have been able
to put an end to it.

65
00:06:53,037 --> 00:06:55,081
I shouldn't be saying this to you.

66
00:06:55,164 --> 00:06:58,793
I should be asking myself that over
and over, as a constant reminder,

67
00:06:59,585 --> 00:07:01,462
as a way of punishing myself.

68
00:07:02,839 --> 00:07:07,385
Dr. Jo, um… Please let me join you, okay?

69
00:07:07,468 --> 00:07:11,013
Uh, what if I assist you?
Tell me what to do and I'll do it, please?

70
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:13,891
Oh, no, not you.

71
00:07:14,976 --> 00:07:17,937
Just let the two of us do it ourselves.

72
00:07:18,771 --> 00:07:20,481
Let us save you from this, okay?

73
00:07:23,359 --> 00:07:26,529
So when this is all through, um…

74
00:07:28,823 --> 00:07:30,616
Park Tae-gyeong will still be here.

75
00:07:38,708 --> 00:07:39,834
Let us do that for you.

76
00:07:43,254 --> 00:07:45,423
Please? Just let us…

77
00:07:47,341 --> 00:07:48,843
let us do this on our own.

78
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:23,878
It's a miracle we made it this far alive,
you and I.

79
00:08:35,598 --> 00:08:40,144
I had them buried… those shoes…

80
00:08:42,355 --> 00:08:44,148
buried with Baraka.

81
00:08:46,859 --> 00:08:48,653
That's when I heard it.

82
00:08:50,154 --> 00:08:52,823
That's when God forgave me.

83
00:08:54,742 --> 00:08:56,661
The children's letters…

84
00:08:58,788 --> 00:09:01,290
Look at the children's letters.

85
00:09:03,125 --> 00:09:04,502
They love me…

86
00:09:05,670 --> 00:09:07,255
those children.

87
00:09:31,988 --> 00:09:32,989
<i>Why?</i>

88
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:35,575
Why did you choose me?

89
00:09:36,367 --> 00:09:41,747
You… always save all of your patients,

90
00:09:43,291 --> 00:09:45,793
no matter who they are.

91
00:09:48,087 --> 00:09:50,423
You're the one most like me.

92
00:09:51,924 --> 00:09:55,094
You're my finest, most brilliant student.

93
00:09:56,220 --> 00:09:58,973
There is no such thing as failure.

94
00:10:00,766 --> 00:10:01,767
That's who…

95
00:10:03,102 --> 00:10:04,562
Gye Su-jeong is.

96
00:10:09,942 --> 00:10:10,943
Right.

97
00:10:13,154 --> 00:10:15,114
That's exactly what I wanted to hear.

98
00:10:54,570 --> 00:10:57,156
No, Gye Su-jeong! Su-jeong.

99
00:11:24,058 --> 00:11:25,059
It's Neema.

100
00:11:35,027 --> 00:11:36,112
"Hello."

101
00:11:36,779 --> 00:11:37,863
Hello.

102
00:11:42,576 --> 00:11:43,411
Heart.

103
00:11:44,245 --> 00:11:48,332
- And this? "Heart."
- My heart.

104
00:12:07,476 --> 00:12:11,188
She doesn't know
how to speak just yet. Not yet.

105
00:12:12,398 --> 00:12:18,696
Still, she wanted to greet you, so
she practiced saying "hello" many times.

106
00:12:19,613 --> 00:12:20,906
Pretty great, isn't it?

107
00:12:22,032 --> 00:12:25,411
You can write your name too,
isn't that right, sweetie?

108
00:12:28,330 --> 00:12:29,999
Amazing, huh?

109
00:12:30,708 --> 00:12:33,335
Look how much she's grown, our Neema.

110
00:12:34,545 --> 00:12:38,507
I brought her here. I asked her to come.

111
00:12:39,759 --> 00:12:41,010
To hold you back.

112
00:12:42,762 --> 00:12:43,596
To…

113
00:12:45,055 --> 00:12:46,724
to keep you from doing this.

114
00:13:27,973 --> 00:13:28,974
What?

115
00:13:29,600 --> 00:13:35,314
Dr. Jang, fancy meeting you here.
Now, please, hand over Neema.

116
00:13:35,397 --> 00:13:36,649
And why should I?

117
00:13:36,732 --> 00:13:38,859
You kidnapped Neema and hid her away.

118
00:13:38,943 --> 00:13:42,988
White Wings Medical Corps is responsible
for her. We've been searching everywhere.

119
00:13:43,072 --> 00:13:45,199
Only because you know she's a witness.

120
00:13:45,282 --> 00:13:49,245
She's the only who knows that you stole
the photos, covered everything up,

121
00:13:49,328 --> 00:13:53,457
- and are trying to frame Su-jeong!
- That's absolutely absurd.

122
00:13:53,541 --> 00:13:55,125
Don't try to deny it.

123
00:13:55,209 --> 00:13:58,379
I know what kind of people you are
better than anyone else on Earth.

124
00:13:58,462 --> 00:14:03,092
Dr. Jang, we're not about to let one
bad apple spoil all of Baba's great works.

125
00:14:05,010 --> 00:14:10,975
Neema. How have you been? You've
been scared, haven't you? It's okay.

126
00:14:11,892 --> 00:14:14,228
Neema. Let's go home.

127
00:14:15,020 --> 00:14:16,397
- Ms. Jang!
- Little doctor!

128
00:14:20,067 --> 00:14:21,402
I'll stop it…

129
00:14:23,988 --> 00:14:27,741
I'll stop the surgery, and Baba will die.

130
00:14:28,617 --> 00:14:30,286
If you lay a finger on Neema…

131
00:14:34,874 --> 00:14:36,458
I won't do anything.

132
00:14:37,501 --> 00:14:39,545
I may be Baba's favorite student,

133
00:14:40,462 --> 00:14:44,550
but Baba is not my teacher.

134
00:14:45,551 --> 00:14:46,385
Go.

135
00:14:47,887 --> 00:14:49,054
No.

136
00:14:50,598 --> 00:14:53,642
Ah… I had a feeling I would find you here.

137
00:14:54,768 --> 00:14:57,813
I just thought that,
since the donor surgery is over,

138
00:14:57,897 --> 00:15:01,859
I'd come find you so I could personally
escort you all to my office.

139
00:15:03,444 --> 00:15:06,447
Oh. Uh, we'd rather stay here--

140
00:15:06,530 --> 00:15:09,241
It's so cramped in here, though.
My office is much nicer.

141
00:15:09,992 --> 00:15:13,120
The surgery will go well.
We should get going now.

142
00:15:35,851 --> 00:15:39,355
Director. Uh, I can't explain
everything right now, but…

143
00:15:39,438 --> 00:15:40,731
Could you help me out?

144
00:15:40,814 --> 00:15:44,443
I promise I'll explain everything later.
I just need your help this one time.

145
00:15:45,736 --> 00:15:46,570
Please.

146
00:16:30,990 --> 00:16:31,949
TURN OFF AFTER USE

147
00:16:32,032 --> 00:16:35,369
Testing, testing.
Oh, sheesh, why isn't this working?

148
00:17:35,095 --> 00:17:38,932
YOU
GUY SU-JEONG

149
00:17:43,187 --> 00:17:45,773
GUY SU-JEONG

150
00:19:11,942 --> 00:19:14,653
All right, let's resume the surgery.

151
00:19:37,217 --> 00:19:38,802
YOU
GUY SU-JEONG

152
00:20:35,359 --> 00:20:38,612
Um, Dr. Jo, you said that
it's good for patients

153
00:20:38,695 --> 00:20:41,657
to listen to music and sounds
that they like…

154
00:20:41,740 --> 00:20:43,283
Dr. Jo, don't worry about it.

155
00:20:44,326 --> 00:20:47,496
At times, Ms. Ju-hye
can be a bit presumptuous.

156
00:20:47,579 --> 00:20:50,165
No, it's fine. It slipped my mind.

157
00:21:11,687 --> 00:21:13,230
Commencing de-airing.

158
00:21:13,313 --> 00:21:17,025
DE-AIRING: REMOVING AIR
FROM BLOOD VESSELS OR THE SURGICAL SITE

159
00:21:24,700 --> 00:21:26,118
I'll lower the head.

160
00:21:27,995 --> 00:21:28,829
Cut, please.

161
00:21:36,920 --> 00:21:38,422
Begin weaning.

162
00:21:38,505 --> 00:21:43,010
WEANING: GRADUALLY REDUCING
VENTILATOR SUPPORT FOR SELF-BREATHING

163
00:22:30,599 --> 00:22:31,683
- I'm sorry.
- It's okay.

164
00:22:32,559 --> 00:22:34,644
She fell asleep.

165
00:22:48,283 --> 00:22:49,534
I'm sorry.

166
00:22:54,081 --> 00:22:57,667
I'm sorry. It's all my fault.

167
00:22:59,211 --> 00:23:00,879
I'm so sorry, Neema.

168
00:23:08,303 --> 00:23:09,554
I owe you an apology.

169
00:23:12,766 --> 00:23:14,184
I'm so sorry.

170
00:23:17,896 --> 00:23:19,106
It's all my fault.

171
00:23:23,527 --> 00:23:24,861
I'm sorry…

172
00:24:00,814 --> 00:24:02,691
Hello, Neema.

173
00:25:24,481 --> 00:25:26,858
- There she is. Neema!
- Neema!

174
00:25:26,942 --> 00:25:29,903
- Neema, we missed you so much.
- We missed you!

175
00:25:29,986 --> 00:25:32,197
Are you okay? Yeah? Three, two, one!

176
00:25:32,280 --> 00:25:33,490
Whoa!

177
00:25:35,408 --> 00:25:38,787
Neema, you're so lucky.
This is Dr. Gye Su-jeong.

178
00:25:38,870 --> 00:25:40,455
- Ah!
- Thank you so much.

179
00:25:43,875 --> 00:25:44,876
Oh…

180
00:25:47,963 --> 00:25:49,214
Thank you for everything.

181
00:25:50,006 --> 00:25:52,133
Neema's so special. Um, thank you.

182
00:25:52,217 --> 00:25:54,553
- Of course.
- She's the best.

183
00:26:18,868 --> 00:26:19,869
Hi, Mom.

184
00:26:41,891 --> 00:26:42,809
Next.

185
00:26:43,643 --> 00:26:48,940
Neema! Hello. Welcome.

186
00:26:49,024 --> 00:26:50,859
- For you.
- Wow.

187
00:27:15,050 --> 00:27:16,551
Two milligrams lorazepam, please.

188
00:27:16,635 --> 00:27:17,719
Okay.

189
00:27:22,265 --> 00:27:24,851
What-- What did you do to me?

190
00:27:29,898 --> 00:27:33,026
Neema… Where is Neema?

191
00:27:36,488 --> 00:27:38,365
How did he know Neema was here?

192
00:27:39,908 --> 00:27:41,034
He was listening.

193
00:27:42,827 --> 00:27:44,204
During the surgery.

194
00:27:51,711 --> 00:27:53,296
Intraoperative awareness…

195
00:27:54,839 --> 00:27:56,091
He was awake.

196
00:28:19,864 --> 00:28:23,284
White Wings Medical Corps
is threatening to sue.

197
00:28:23,368 --> 00:28:25,245
Do you have something to say?

198
00:28:27,163 --> 00:28:30,208
Couldn't you just check
the CCTV footage, Director?

199
00:28:31,000 --> 00:28:33,795
That won't be enough.
And as you know, per hospital rules,

200
00:28:33,878 --> 00:28:36,131
all those who participated in the surgery

201
00:28:36,214 --> 00:28:38,842
must give their consent for us
to watch the footage.

202
00:28:38,925 --> 00:28:41,761
As for Ms. Ju-hye and I,
neither one of us saw anything.

203
00:28:41,845 --> 00:28:44,139
We were only looking at the surgical site.

204
00:28:44,222 --> 00:28:46,307
We have nothing more to say about that.

205
00:28:48,935 --> 00:28:53,440
Dr. Park Tae-gyeong. You have
something to tell me, don't you?

206
00:28:55,608 --> 00:28:56,860
Uh…

207
00:28:58,236 --> 00:29:00,572
Yes, yes, I do. I'll tell you.

208
00:29:00,655 --> 00:29:02,615
Dr. Park Tae-gyeong doesn't know anything.

209
00:29:02,699 --> 00:29:04,826
Meaning that you, on the other hand, do?

210
00:29:05,952 --> 00:29:10,665
I'm Dr. Kim Seung-hyo's family. White
Wings has no right to sue the hospital.

211
00:29:11,750 --> 00:29:15,795
The surgery went well. His waking up
during the surgery was unfortunate,

212
00:29:15,879 --> 00:29:19,048
but as the anesthesiologist,
it's my responsibility.

213
00:29:19,132 --> 00:29:21,176
So I'm the one they would have to sue.

214
00:29:23,094 --> 00:29:27,182
Would he sue his own daughter?
The great humanitarian,

215
00:29:27,265 --> 00:29:29,559
the honorable Dr. Kim Seung-hyo?

216
00:29:36,441 --> 00:29:37,817
Show those two out, please.

217
00:29:48,536 --> 00:29:50,914
The patient was awake from the very start,

218
00:29:50,997 --> 00:29:54,125
so the BIS monitor readings
must have indicated a change.

219
00:29:54,793 --> 00:29:58,505
However, somehow
the monitor got turned off.

220
00:29:59,714 --> 00:30:01,758
I also took a look at the medication log.

221
00:30:03,051 --> 00:30:04,552
I noticed that the flumazenil,

222
00:30:04,636 --> 00:30:06,471
the awakening agent,

223
00:30:06,554 --> 00:30:09,265
that was dispensed,
was twice the usual amount,

224
00:30:09,349 --> 00:30:12,644
but it was returned in its entirety
without being used.

225
00:30:17,732 --> 00:30:19,567
Why would you do something like that?

226
00:30:21,194 --> 00:30:23,238
Why would you wake him up

227
00:30:24,322 --> 00:30:25,907
during his surgery?

228
00:30:30,036 --> 00:30:31,621
Let me rephrase the question.

229
00:30:34,415 --> 00:30:37,335
What changed your mind?

230
00:30:53,476 --> 00:30:57,856
How dare you…
How dare you call yourself a doctor.

231
00:30:59,315 --> 00:31:00,733
Great humanitarian?

232
00:31:01,860 --> 00:31:03,403
How could you do that?

233
00:31:16,541 --> 00:31:17,792
Pupils are dilated.

234
00:31:19,669 --> 00:31:20,753
Director Bu.

235
00:31:22,213 --> 00:31:23,381
We need to tell you something.

236
00:31:23,464 --> 00:31:25,091
They're shutting us down, huh?

237
00:31:25,174 --> 00:31:27,510
They haven't made
an official announcement yet,

238
00:31:27,594 --> 00:31:29,429
but the news will be made public soon.

239
00:31:29,512 --> 00:31:32,599
And they're going to sell the land?
So, do we know that for sure?

240
00:31:32,682 --> 00:31:34,183
According to the reporter,

241
00:31:34,267 --> 00:31:39,188
Chairman Gu Bon-pyeong has already met
with several developers to discuss it.

242
00:31:39,272 --> 00:31:41,566
That's why it's been so quiet here lately.

243
00:31:41,649 --> 00:31:44,068
I was wondering why Kim Chang-su
and the mayor weren't here

244
00:31:44,152 --> 00:31:48,197
getting their pictures taken and giving
interviews about Kim Seung-hyo's surgery.

245
00:31:48,281 --> 00:31:50,783
They're just too busy. Ugh!

246
00:31:51,534 --> 00:31:54,203
During COVID, we worked
so hard to keep this place afloat.

247
00:31:54,829 --> 00:31:57,540
This whole area would have been
devastated if it weren't for our hospital.

248
00:31:57,624 --> 00:32:01,336
So all that work we put into proving
ourselves was futile, right?

249
00:32:01,419 --> 00:32:03,087
During the strike, they probably thought,

250
00:32:03,171 --> 00:32:06,299
"Man, it's so empty in here,
I guess we actually can sell this place."

251
00:32:07,550 --> 00:32:13,056
Even so… shouldn't we at least make
some sort of effort to save the hospital?

252
00:32:17,018 --> 00:32:18,436
You can't get a hold of anyone?

253
00:32:19,228 --> 00:32:23,066
No. Not the mayor, the chairman,
or the people around them.

254
00:32:24,859 --> 00:32:26,945
I'll find out when
Magnolia's next meeting is.

255
00:33:04,941 --> 00:33:06,192
Oh, Dr. Park.

256
00:33:07,735 --> 00:33:08,653
Why are we here?

257
00:33:10,071 --> 00:33:10,947
- Uh…
- Hmm?

258
00:33:21,624 --> 00:33:22,667
Look…

259
00:34:09,922 --> 00:34:12,884
Uh, you should take a look
where she drew it.

260
00:34:12,967 --> 00:34:17,221
It's right next to the place
where you were performing surgery.

261
00:35:19,826 --> 00:35:22,078
My parents know. I told them everything.

262
00:35:30,086 --> 00:35:31,420
MOM: MY DEAR TAE-GYEONG…

263
00:35:38,553 --> 00:35:41,514
GOD WILL ALWAYS BE WITH YOU. HE IS THERE
WHEREVER THERE IS LOVE. WE LOVE YOU.

264
00:35:51,023 --> 00:35:53,109
They thanked me for persevering,

265
00:35:55,653 --> 00:35:57,405
and not giving up on this world.

266
00:36:04,912 --> 00:36:06,038
So now I'll…

267
00:36:07,999 --> 00:36:09,917
I'll do my best to be brave.

268
00:36:35,693 --> 00:36:37,778
Do you think God exists?

269
00:36:41,991 --> 00:36:43,784
Would it matter if He did?

270
00:36:45,203 --> 00:36:46,913
Do you believe in God?

271
00:36:52,084 --> 00:36:53,252
I hate Him.

272
00:36:55,588 --> 00:36:56,714
Hmm…

273
00:36:59,634 --> 00:37:03,304
Well… God believes in you.

274
00:37:06,849 --> 00:37:09,060
I guess that's why
He stopped by down there.

275
00:37:10,686 --> 00:37:12,813
"Leave me to deal with him.

276
00:37:13,397 --> 00:37:15,566
You just carry on doing your work.

277
00:37:17,735 --> 00:37:18,819
Be a doctor…

278
00:37:19,946 --> 00:37:21,447
just a little while longer."

279
00:37:42,802 --> 00:37:44,929
Ugh! This won't work, no way.

280
00:37:48,307 --> 00:37:52,186
I don't think it's all gonna fit.
Problem is…

281
00:37:53,771 --> 00:37:55,356
I can't part with any of them.

282
00:37:55,439 --> 00:37:58,442
Yeah, I knew it, so I bought a bag too.

283
00:37:58,526 --> 00:38:02,405
I'll go get it. We got this…

284
00:38:04,031 --> 00:38:07,535
Hey, you're really not going back to work?

285
00:38:16,377 --> 00:38:18,087
I'm not sure if it'd be okay or not.

286
00:38:19,839 --> 00:38:21,424
I don't know if I'm allowed…

287
00:38:23,509 --> 00:38:24,969
to be a doctor again.

288
00:38:26,762 --> 00:38:30,808
Neema's foster parents
applied to adopt her.

289
00:38:32,977 --> 00:38:38,107
Neema's over the moon about it, too.
You have a family now!

290
00:38:41,152 --> 00:38:42,320
I'll go get the bag.

291
00:38:49,910 --> 00:38:50,870
Hey.

292
00:38:55,291 --> 00:38:57,668
I saw the drawing on the glass.

293
00:39:09,847 --> 00:39:11,223
I saw Baraka too.

294
00:39:13,851 --> 00:39:14,977
Thank you.

295
00:40:07,321 --> 00:40:11,367
<i>Oh, my love, magnolia </i>

296
00:40:11,450 --> 00:40:12,451
Oh!

297
00:40:13,869 --> 00:40:17,415
We've been sitting here
forever. And nobody has spoken to us.

298
00:40:19,083 --> 00:40:24,672
<i>Today and tomorrow </i>

299
00:40:24,755 --> 00:40:30,678
- <i>I will live beautifully forever</i>
- Thank you so much.

300
00:40:32,805 --> 00:40:36,434
It seems Director Kim Myeong-seop
knew about it a while ago.

301
00:40:36,517 --> 00:40:38,394
Sorry? Knew what?

302
00:40:38,477 --> 00:40:41,230
He always knew that
we'd be cast aside like this.

303
00:40:42,231 --> 00:40:43,357
That's why he let me have it.

304
00:40:44,608 --> 00:40:46,152
He knew I'd be out eventually.

305
00:40:46,235 --> 00:40:49,321
That makes sense.
He gave up the fight way too easily.

306
00:40:49,905 --> 00:40:52,408
Still, we're the only major hospital
in the area.

307
00:40:53,033 --> 00:40:55,744
We could've accomplished so many things.

308
00:40:56,787 --> 00:41:00,040
I believe that song gave us
healthcare workers great courage

309
00:41:00,124 --> 00:41:02,084
in this bitter winter we're facing.

310
00:41:03,294 --> 00:41:09,175
Now, let's see…
which number is up next. All right.

311
00:41:12,678 --> 00:41:15,347
We have to talk to them.
It's gonna be over soon.

312
00:41:15,431 --> 00:41:19,059
How are we gonna change their minds
if we don't start a conversation at least?

313
00:41:19,143 --> 00:41:21,854
And we'll go to…

314
00:41:24,982 --> 00:41:27,818
- Hmm, hmm…
- You're right. I'll go over right now.

315
00:41:28,569 --> 00:41:30,154
Number 19!

316
00:41:33,032 --> 00:41:35,993
The previous number
was a classical art song,

317
00:41:36,076 --> 00:41:39,455
so how about we liven things up
with something upbeat?

318
00:41:39,538 --> 00:41:42,458
Oh, you're already on your feet,
number 19.

319
00:41:43,250 --> 00:41:48,172
Director Bu Seung-gwon of the famous
Guseo University Seonam Medical Center.

320
00:41:51,467 --> 00:41:53,344
Take me instead.

321
00:41:54,220 --> 00:41:56,263
Everyone, give him a round of applause!

322
00:42:03,020 --> 00:42:06,649
We've all really been looking forward
to this, especially Chairman Gu.

323
00:42:06,732 --> 00:42:09,860
If you want a chance to have a drink
with him and chat afterward,

324
00:42:09,944 --> 00:42:11,654
you really better make this good.

325
00:42:12,571 --> 00:42:14,073
Especially you, Director Bu.

326
00:42:14,156 --> 00:42:18,285
If you wanna make up for that huge mistake
you made, you'll need to do something.

327
00:42:18,369 --> 00:42:20,204
You should at least dance
if you can't sing.

328
00:42:33,676 --> 00:42:34,552
Ah, damn it!

329
00:42:34,635 --> 00:42:37,680
Dr. Do, what are you… Wait, don't go up--

330
00:42:39,682 --> 00:42:41,433
Ah, this is…

331
00:42:46,480 --> 00:42:49,024
<i>One, four, two, four, six.</i>

332
00:42:50,609 --> 00:42:51,443
All right!

333
00:42:51,527 --> 00:42:52,778
"BINGO"
SONG BY: TURTLES

334
00:42:54,905 --> 00:42:58,534
<i>Ladies and gentlemen</i>
<i>Oh, yeah, I'm back again </i>

335
00:42:58,617 --> 00:43:01,120
<i>Yes, I'm back again I feel so good</i>

336
00:43:01,203 --> 00:43:02,204
Director.

337
00:43:02,288 --> 00:43:08,669
<i>Let me sing a song first</i>
<i>Feeling so happy I'm about to burst… </i>

338
00:43:08,752 --> 00:43:10,713
Huh? Hey, wait, you can't leave.

339
00:43:12,715 --> 00:43:16,218
<i>If I start again on pure grit </i>

340
00:43:16,302 --> 00:43:19,805
<i>I'll accomplish everything I desire </i>

341
00:43:19,888 --> 00:43:23,434
<i>I love the land</i>
<i>I'm living in right now… </i>

342
00:43:26,270 --> 00:43:29,398
Aw, damn it! Geez!

343
00:44:39,385 --> 00:44:43,055
<i>After much speculation,</i>
<i>Guseo University Seonam Medical Center</i>

344
00:44:43,138 --> 00:44:45,140
<i>will be closing its doors in September.</i>

345
00:44:45,224 --> 00:44:47,476
<i>The institution has</i>
<i>a long history and tradition,</i>

346
00:44:47,559 --> 00:44:51,689
<i>and has served as a key branch hospital</i>
<i>of Guseo University Medical Center.</i>

347
00:44:51,772 --> 00:44:53,607
<i>We go now to our reporter</i>
<i>on the scene for more details…</i>

348
00:44:53,691 --> 00:44:55,359
END THE DOCTORS' STRIKE.
WE CONDEMN DOUBLE STANDARDS.

349
00:44:55,442 --> 00:44:57,027
A little to the right, Ms. Ju-hye.

350
00:44:57,111 --> 00:44:59,321
<i>The Guseo Foundation announced that</i>

351
00:44:59,405 --> 00:45:01,323
<i>- Guseo University Seonam Medical Center…</i>
- Ms. Ju-hye.

352
00:45:01,407 --> 00:45:03,575
<i>…will be closing.</i>
<i>They cited mounting deficits,</i>

353
00:45:03,659 --> 00:45:05,577
<i>the cost of modernizing medical systems,</i>

354
00:45:05,661 --> 00:45:08,622
<i>and staffing shortages</i>
<i>as reasons for the closure.</i>

355
00:45:08,706 --> 00:45:10,916
<i>Some have suggested</i>
<i>that the prolonged residents' strike</i>

356
00:45:10,999 --> 00:45:13,043
<i>and medical students' leave of absence</i>

357
00:45:13,127 --> 00:45:15,713
<i>helped hasten the decision</i>
<i>to close the hospital.</i>

358
00:45:15,796 --> 00:45:17,297
<i>Breaking news.</i>

359
00:45:17,381 --> 00:45:20,509
<i>An alleged victim came forward</i>
<i>claiming that Dr. Kim Seung-hyo,</i>

360
00:45:20,592 --> 00:45:23,220
<i>humanitarian leader of</i>
<i>White Wings Medical Corps,</i>

361
00:45:23,303 --> 00:45:25,264
<i>sexually assaulted them as a child.</i>

362
00:45:25,347 --> 00:45:28,100
<i>Testimonies and revelations</i>
<i>are now surfacing.</i>

363
00:45:28,183 --> 00:45:30,102
<i>The victims claim</i>
<i>they were sexually assaulted</i>

364
00:45:30,185 --> 00:45:32,312
<i>under the guise of playing doctor,</i>

365
00:45:32,396 --> 00:45:35,399
<i>and the release of a photo album</i>
<i>that belonged to Dr. Kim Seung-hyo</i>

366
00:45:35,482 --> 00:45:37,151
<i>has also caused outrage.</i>

367
00:45:37,234 --> 00:45:39,027
<i>This is Jeong Ga-ram reporting.</i>

368
00:45:39,111 --> 00:45:41,905
<i>This album is filled</i>
<i>with photos of numerous children.</i>

369
00:45:41,989 --> 00:45:45,033
<i>It contains only photos of children.</i>

370
00:45:45,117 --> 00:45:47,995
<i>The album, which was provided</i>
<i>by an anonymous source,</i>

371
00:45:48,078 --> 00:45:50,122
<i>belongs to Dr. Kim Seung-hyo.</i>

372
00:45:50,205 --> 00:45:53,500
<i>Most of the children in the photos</i>
<i>have been identified</i>

373
00:45:53,584 --> 00:45:56,420
<i>as the children in the refugee camp</i>
<i>run by White Wings.</i>

374
00:45:56,503 --> 00:45:58,922
<i>White Wings claims the photos</i>
<i>are physical exam records…</i>

375
00:46:04,303 --> 00:46:06,013
SYSTEM SHUTTING DOWN

376
00:46:13,771 --> 00:46:17,983
It's been so long since we've had
a meal together. It was nice.

377
00:46:18,066 --> 00:46:19,610
I'll come by to eat often.

378
00:46:19,693 --> 00:46:22,029
Let's live in this hell forever,
you and I.

379
00:46:22,863 --> 00:46:25,449
How about it, Dad? You up for it?

380
00:46:50,474 --> 00:46:54,394
A farewell party…
You guys really didn't have to do this.

381
00:46:54,478 --> 00:46:57,648
We didn't actually.
We just felt like having a drink.

382
00:46:58,649 --> 00:47:01,151
And we thought we'd invite
you and Gye Su-jeong along.

383
00:47:01,235 --> 00:47:06,365
You know, when we would say to you, "Go,
please get out of here," you never would.

384
00:47:07,241 --> 00:47:10,828
And now that we're short staffed and
begging you to join us, you won't do it?

385
00:47:10,911 --> 00:47:12,496
Are you kidding me?

386
00:47:12,579 --> 00:47:16,834
Paid vacations, benefits, half days,
do I get stuff like that?

387
00:47:16,917 --> 00:47:19,586
Or some incentive or something?

388
00:47:19,670 --> 00:47:21,630
You're just a temp, you don't get those.

389
00:47:22,256 --> 00:47:24,258
And you, your internship is over now

390
00:47:24,341 --> 00:47:27,219
so you'd better not go off
and forget all of us you left behind.

391
00:47:27,302 --> 00:47:30,222
Oh, no, I would never do that.
I wouldn't dare.

392
00:47:33,892 --> 00:47:34,893
Uh, Director.

393
00:47:34,977 --> 00:47:37,688
Hey! Tonight,
you should be drinking too, Director.

394
00:47:37,771 --> 00:47:40,107
Go ahead and order, it's my treat.
No, I got it. I got it. I got it.

395
00:47:40,190 --> 00:47:42,442
No, tonight the food is on me.

396
00:47:42,526 --> 00:47:43,735
No, it's on me.

397
00:47:44,486 --> 00:47:49,157
Because Dr. Park Tae-gyeong and I
are both graduating.

398
00:47:53,537 --> 00:47:55,873
- Okay, let's toast.
- Sounds good.

399
00:47:57,249 --> 00:48:00,085
Ah, well, this is a first,
all of us drinking together.

400
00:48:00,168 --> 00:48:01,837
All right, come on. Here we go.

401
00:48:02,421 --> 00:48:04,131
Cheers!

402
00:48:04,214 --> 00:48:05,424
To all of us!

403
00:48:07,175 --> 00:48:09,386
<i>Director Bu decided to retire.</i>

404
00:48:09,469 --> 00:48:11,513
<i>With the hospital officially closing…</i>

405
00:48:11,597 --> 00:48:14,850
<i>…he had no reason or energy</i>
<i>to hold on any longer.</i>

406
00:48:14,933 --> 00:48:18,770
<i>His retirement ceremony will be held</i>
<i>in the event hall in five days.</i>

407
00:48:18,854 --> 00:48:20,564
<i>We're going to make it a grand event.</i>

408
00:48:20,647 --> 00:48:22,274
Another toast! To me going on a date.

409
00:48:22,357 --> 00:48:27,237
<i>And us as well, this trio of GS lackeys,</i>

410
00:48:27,321 --> 00:48:28,780
<i>we're graduating, too.</i>

411
00:48:30,073 --> 00:48:33,452
I didn't think
they'd actually close the hospital.

412
00:48:33,535 --> 00:48:37,331
The mayor is gonna change the zoning
to business and retail.

413
00:48:38,248 --> 00:48:41,543
They'll demolish the hospital
and build something profitable.

414
00:48:41,627 --> 00:48:45,172
But still, our hospital was
the only one in that whole area.

415
00:48:46,548 --> 00:48:50,218
Hey, we did the best we could do.

416
00:48:51,011 --> 00:48:52,596
You don't believe me, do you?

417
00:48:53,138 --> 00:48:57,851
Probably not. The way we saw it, we were…

418
00:48:59,227 --> 00:49:02,940
We were trying our best to do
what we could. We really did try.

419
00:49:04,399 --> 00:49:07,361
I'm sorry for causing so much trouble.

420
00:49:07,986 --> 00:49:13,075
Our Park Tae-gyeong!
You troublemaker, you little, you…

421
00:49:13,158 --> 00:49:16,745
You know, you're the guy…
you're the guy I'll never forget.

422
00:49:16,828 --> 00:49:19,289
You hear me? Are you okay?

423
00:49:21,917 --> 00:49:23,627
Director Bu drank a lot.

424
00:49:23,710 --> 00:49:26,088
Mm-hmm.

425
00:49:26,171 --> 00:49:28,256
Oh, Director.

426
00:49:30,217 --> 00:49:31,426
Oh…

427
00:49:36,723 --> 00:49:39,935
Oh, uh, I'll go get you
some hangover cure.

428
00:49:40,936 --> 00:49:42,437
Dr. Park Tae-gyeong.

429
00:49:44,189 --> 00:49:45,691
You've worked very hard.

430
00:49:51,321 --> 00:49:56,284
Not hard enough. I was so inadequate.
I'm sorry about everything.

431
00:49:59,246 --> 00:50:04,376
No, I'm the one who's sorry.
I was the inadequate one.

432
00:50:06,461 --> 00:50:07,713
All of you…

433
00:50:08,296 --> 00:50:09,965
have been through a lot…

434
00:50:12,009 --> 00:50:13,760
because of my inadequacies…

435
00:50:16,805 --> 00:50:19,433
Whoa, whoa, whoa, Director. Not at all.

436
00:50:20,350 --> 00:50:22,561
Oh, come on, don't say that.

437
00:50:22,644 --> 00:50:25,439
Okay, since you're up,
why don't you take a minute

438
00:50:25,522 --> 00:50:29,067
to say some encouraging words
to Dr. Park Tae-gyeong?

439
00:50:32,362 --> 00:50:35,782
- I think I wanna sing a song.
- Huh?

440
00:50:35,866 --> 00:50:39,703
Instead of just giving
some boring speech, I'll--

441
00:50:41,580 --> 00:50:42,789
I'll sing you a song.

442
00:50:42,873 --> 00:50:44,332
You sure?

443
00:50:55,635 --> 00:51:00,098
<i>The frozen shadow </i>

444
00:51:01,058 --> 00:51:05,562
<i>Of the moon </i>

445
00:51:06,813 --> 00:51:12,194
<i>Rests upon </i>

446
00:51:12,277 --> 00:51:15,155
<i>The waves </i>

447
00:51:16,156 --> 00:51:20,243
<i>In the cold winter </i>

448
00:51:21,495 --> 00:51:25,999
<i>A small island </i>

449
00:51:27,000 --> 00:51:30,629
<i>Stands alone </i>

450
00:51:30,712 --> 00:51:34,800
<i>Against the raging sea </i>

451
00:51:36,718 --> 00:51:40,889
<i>Remember </i>

452
00:51:41,932 --> 00:51:44,935
- <i>The keeper…</i>
- <i>Hyeon-a, it's Dad.</i>

453
00:51:45,018 --> 00:51:47,771
<i>- Hello, Dad!</i>
- Hi, Hyeon-a!

454
00:51:47,854 --> 00:51:50,482
- Are you coming home soon?
<i>- I'm still working.</i>

455
00:51:50,565 --> 00:51:52,734
<i>…of that lighthouse </i>

456
00:52:07,374 --> 00:52:08,458
Are you…

457
00:52:09,459 --> 00:52:10,752
still going to be a doctor?

458
00:52:10,836 --> 00:52:12,838
I have the same question for you.

459
00:52:14,422 --> 00:52:18,468
Gye Su-jeong,
are you still going to be a doctor?

460
00:52:23,265 --> 00:52:24,808
Are you retiring for real?

461
00:52:27,018 --> 00:52:27,853
Yeah.

462
00:52:29,604 --> 00:52:33,567
I thought I was a lighthouse keeper,
you know?

463
00:52:35,026 --> 00:52:36,111
But it turns out…

464
00:52:37,320 --> 00:52:39,906
I was just a ship that lost its way.

465
00:52:46,037 --> 00:52:49,457
A lost ship, or even
a sinking ship for that matter…

466
00:52:50,292 --> 00:52:53,712
still needs to have a captain.

467
00:52:55,589 --> 00:52:56,756
You're not saying…

468
00:52:58,466 --> 00:53:00,760
I should go down with the ship, are you?

469
00:53:01,344 --> 00:53:05,307
Regardless of any obstacles, a captain
guides everyone safely to shore,

470
00:53:06,558 --> 00:53:10,478
and I think…
that's what being a Director is all about.

471
00:53:21,948 --> 00:53:26,995
Oh, you picked that one,
the most expensive one.

472
00:53:59,069 --> 00:54:01,738
- Get in. Aren't you all going to work?
- Yeah, but…

473
00:54:04,407 --> 00:54:06,785
All right,
you can take me to work, I guess.

474
00:54:06,868 --> 00:54:10,455
I need to go to work
if I wanna replace this bucket of bolts.

475
00:54:10,538 --> 00:54:13,792
That hunk of junk is pretty much new
after all the repairs it's had.

476
00:54:14,292 --> 00:54:15,835
- Okay.
- Oh.

477
00:54:15,919 --> 00:54:19,881
I think I'm gonna jog.
It's not too far and it's been a while.

478
00:54:19,965 --> 00:54:23,593
Hey, wait a second, Su-jeong,
since when have you been a jogger?

479
00:54:23,677 --> 00:54:26,221
If we die, we die together.
If we live, we live together.

480
00:54:26,304 --> 00:54:27,806
- All for one!
- Come on!

481
00:54:30,016 --> 00:54:31,851
- Get in.
- Let's go.

482
00:54:31,935 --> 00:54:35,480
Hey, this is the first time
since we opened the agency

483
00:54:35,563 --> 00:54:37,857
that all of us are going
to work together, you know?

484
00:54:37,941 --> 00:54:39,526
Okay, seat belts!

485
00:54:39,609 --> 00:54:41,444
- Okay, seat belt…
- Seat belt, Su-jeong.

486
00:54:41,528 --> 00:54:42,696
All right!

487
00:54:42,779 --> 00:54:44,739
- I'm good.
- Ready? Let's go!

488
00:54:44,823 --> 00:54:46,700
- Hold on tight!
- Let's do this!

489
00:54:46,783 --> 00:54:49,411
Oh, oh, oh, oh. Oh, oh, oh.

490
00:55:07,679 --> 00:55:09,889
DIRECTOR BU SEUNG-GWON RETIREMENT CEREMONY

491
00:55:15,729 --> 00:55:18,356
HAVE YOU CONSIDERED WORKING OVERSEAS?
"I'M GIVING IT SERIOUS THOUGHT"

492
00:55:26,865 --> 00:55:28,908
K-MEDICINE
EVERYTHING ABOUT WORKING ABROAD

493
00:55:29,701 --> 00:55:31,995
HOSTED BY:
SEONAM MEDICAL ASSOCIATION, MAGNOLIA

494
00:55:37,250 --> 00:55:40,420
- I knew you'd be coming around.
- You scared me to death.

495
00:55:47,594 --> 00:55:49,012
Just heading home or quitting?

496
00:55:50,972 --> 00:55:51,931
I'm quitting.

497
00:55:52,015 --> 00:55:56,269
Ah… At last. We should celebrate.

498
00:55:56,353 --> 00:55:59,439
Wanna do a team dinner tonight?
Oh, I got night duty.

499
00:56:00,857 --> 00:56:02,942
Hey, how do you feel about quitting
on Wednesday?

500
00:56:03,026 --> 00:56:04,402
I can leave early that day.

501
00:56:04,486 --> 00:56:06,196
Let's say our goodbyes here,

502
00:56:06,279 --> 00:56:08,907
in the setting that feels most like
Kim Seong-jin.

503
00:56:12,911 --> 00:56:16,998
Hmm. Who knew you could be
so sentimental? I'm very proud.

504
00:56:18,416 --> 00:56:21,086
I'm gonna save you
in my phone as "Fun Won-jin".

505
00:56:21,628 --> 00:56:23,296
I heard you'll be going
to the main hospital.

506
00:56:23,380 --> 00:56:25,256
- I don't think so.
- Why not?

507
00:56:26,049 --> 00:56:27,634
I'm looking into regional hospitals.

508
00:56:27,717 --> 00:56:31,763
A genius like me is needed mostly in rural
areas where there aren't any doctors.

509
00:56:33,556 --> 00:56:36,393
I know that look, okay?
"Kim Seong-jin is so cool"?

510
00:56:36,476 --> 00:56:37,644
I know, I know. I'm pretty used to it.

511
00:56:37,727 --> 00:56:40,688
That's not it. It's my concerned look.

512
00:56:40,772 --> 00:56:44,067
It means, "If he moves to the country,
he'll be calling and texting even more.

513
00:56:44,150 --> 00:56:45,360
I need to stop this."

514
00:56:45,443 --> 00:56:48,029
No, not at all. I'll be super busy
and super popular there.

515
00:56:48,113 --> 00:56:49,781
The elderly will absolutely love me.

516
00:56:49,864 --> 00:56:51,950
And my best friends
will be farmers and ranchers.

517
00:56:52,033 --> 00:56:53,660
Okay, okay, whatever you say.

518
00:57:01,209 --> 00:57:05,338
The rescue workers and firefighters say
that there's still a good doctor

519
00:57:05,422 --> 00:57:08,341
on the first floor of
Guseo University Medical Center.

520
00:57:09,467 --> 00:57:12,095
It's a shame
that doctor won't be here anymore.

521
00:57:14,889 --> 00:57:19,144
All the patients you've saved over
the years are very grateful for you.

522
00:57:19,853 --> 00:57:22,897
You should be very proud,
Dr. Kim Seong -jin.

523
00:57:27,902 --> 00:57:28,903
Uh…

524
00:57:30,488 --> 00:57:32,532
No matter what people are saying,

525
00:57:33,533 --> 00:57:38,371
whether you're Kim Won-jin or Jo Won-jin,
to me, you are…

526
00:57:39,122 --> 00:57:40,373
just Fun Won-jin.

527
00:57:45,670 --> 00:57:46,880
You wanna go too?

528
00:57:51,843 --> 00:57:55,346
Once I decide where I'm going,
do you wanna go too?

529
00:58:04,230 --> 00:58:06,566
Where exactly? You mean over there?

530
00:58:06,649 --> 00:58:07,817
- Oh. Okay.
- Get over there.

531
00:58:07,901 --> 00:58:11,279
Hey, I'm gonna start a group chat
with you, Dr. Gye, and Park Tae-gyeong

532
00:58:11,362 --> 00:58:13,072
called "Kim Seong-jin and GyeParkJo."

533
00:58:13,156 --> 00:58:16,117
Catchy, right? Hey, I'll invite you.
You can't leave it, okay?

534
00:58:24,584 --> 00:58:26,794
Instead of quitting,
you just went over there?

535
00:58:28,129 --> 00:58:30,089
Yeah, that's how it turned out.

536
00:58:30,173 --> 00:58:31,841
You think I took him because I wanted to?

537
00:58:33,968 --> 00:58:36,679
I had no choice
because it was destiny, Dr. Park.

538
00:58:36,763 --> 00:58:39,140
Come on, that's a bit much,
don't you think?

539
00:58:39,224 --> 00:58:41,184
Dr. Kim is joining Director Bu
for his rounds?

540
00:58:41,267 --> 00:58:42,936
I guess this place really is closing down.

541
00:58:43,019 --> 00:58:47,065
Oh, I just came by to express my gratitude
for him opening up the ER.

542
00:58:47,148 --> 00:58:49,442
Ah, here he comes.

543
00:58:49,526 --> 00:58:51,861
- Stand still.
- <i>The doors are opening.</i>

544
00:59:09,587 --> 00:59:13,132
<i>Director Bu Seung-gwon</i>
<i>will now begin his rounds.</i>

545
00:59:24,811 --> 00:59:27,272
- Dr. Jo.
- Oh, Ms. Jang.

546
00:59:27,355 --> 00:59:29,274
Did you come to work with Dr. Gye?

547
00:59:29,357 --> 00:59:32,652
Oh, I just need to keep an eye
on Su-jeong today, that's all.

548
00:59:32,735 --> 00:59:33,736
Ah…

549
00:59:34,946 --> 00:59:38,283
Oh, so I heard
that you're traveling to Lagota.

550
00:59:42,370 --> 00:59:44,622
And I heard that you resigned,
is that right?

551
00:59:45,540 --> 00:59:46,541
Yeah.

552
00:59:48,418 --> 00:59:51,546
- Then hello, Dr. Jo Won-jin.
- Hi there.

553
00:59:52,463 --> 00:59:55,675
I'm Jang Hui-suk,
from Locum Tenens Agency. Here's my card.

554
00:59:56,509 --> 00:59:59,554
You've now become our agency's
top candidate for recruitment.

555
00:59:59,637 --> 01:00:03,266
Think about it, and when I return,
maybe we can talk.

556
01:00:03,349 --> 01:00:05,852
Or, better yet,
come along with me to Lagota.

557
01:00:05,935 --> 01:00:07,562
Thanks for the offer.

558
01:00:08,354 --> 01:00:09,856
- Just think about it.
- Sure.

559
01:00:25,288 --> 01:00:26,831
That nasty stuff…

560
01:00:26,914 --> 01:00:28,916
that crape myrtle, it's… Ugh.

561
01:00:33,463 --> 01:00:38,926
- So nasty…
- Oh, well, now you know that I…

562
01:00:39,010 --> 01:00:41,679
- I was Ms. Jang's ears at the hospital.
- Hmm?

563
01:00:53,149 --> 01:00:54,108
This is…

564
01:00:55,318 --> 01:00:56,861
a really nice place you've got.

565
01:00:57,487 --> 01:01:00,990
I could've come to your office.
Why bother coming all the way out here?

566
01:01:01,074 --> 01:01:04,327
I want to hire Dr. Gye Su-jeong
to work full-time at the hospital.

567
01:01:06,704 --> 01:01:09,540
I don't mean to be rude,
but I can't send her to work at a hospital

568
01:01:09,624 --> 01:01:12,168
when I know that
it's about to close its doors.

569
01:01:12,251 --> 01:01:14,629
If that does happen, I'll do what it takes

570
01:01:14,712 --> 01:01:16,506
to make sure the main hospital
takes her on.

571
01:01:19,175 --> 01:01:21,761
Is it a deal, Ms. Jang?

572
01:01:22,428 --> 01:01:23,388
The salary…

573
01:01:24,764 --> 01:01:25,973
is that negotiable?

574
01:01:30,603 --> 01:01:31,521
It's a deal.

575
01:01:36,317 --> 01:01:39,570
Oh, but of course,
it's Dr. Gye's choice, ultimately.

576
01:01:46,577 --> 01:01:48,287
So, you'll be joining us?

577
01:01:54,585 --> 01:01:58,005
GYE SU-JEONG

578
01:02:46,721 --> 01:02:51,350
Hello? Okay, on my way.
It's an emergency! Come on, Intern, hurry!

579
01:02:51,434 --> 01:02:52,518
Right!

580
01:03:03,905 --> 01:03:06,574
Yeah. You made the right choice.

581
01:03:08,034 --> 01:03:09,911
You go, Gye Su-jeong.

582
01:03:14,832 --> 01:03:16,209
I'll see you later, Ms. Jang.

583
01:03:44,237 --> 01:03:46,656
<i>This is the story of a lone wolf.</i>

584
01:03:48,032 --> 01:03:52,203
<i>She rebukes being part of the pack</i>
<i>and despises standing authority.</i>

585
01:03:52,286 --> 01:03:55,873
<i>The only weapons stored in her arsenal</i>
<i>are her medical license,</i>

586
01:03:55,957 --> 01:03:59,085
<i>and the surgical skills</i>
<i>that she sharpened from bare metal.</i>

587
01:03:59,168 --> 01:04:00,795
<i>Doctor X.</i>

588
01:04:01,462 --> 01:04:02,922
<i>Also known as…</i>

589
01:04:03,589 --> 01:04:07,051
<i>general surgeon, Gye Su-jeong.</i>

590
01:04:07,134 --> 01:04:10,054
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

591
01:04:10,137 --> 01:04:13,558
SPECIAL THANKS TO KIM WON-HAE AND
JANG SEUNG-JO FOR THEIR GUEST APPEARANCES

